    },
    {
      "text": "Cyber results show small gains over Grok 4.5: CyberGym is 79.7% versus 79.0%, CVE-Bench is 39.8% versus 35.2%, and SecureCodeReview is 58.7% versus 49.4%, with capability probes run without production safeguards.",
      "pages": [29, 30],
      "document": "xai-grok-4-6"
    },
    {
      "text": "HackerBench v0.2 with release safeguards reports 6.9% harmful or dual-use compliance and 0.0% benign refusal.",
      "pages": [31],
      "document": "xai-grok-4-6"
    },
    {
      "text": "Biology and chemistry remain below FAIF thresholds; VCT rises to 67.4%, Biosecurity VCT to 47.8%, BioUseBench severity-5 refusal to 90.7%, and LAB-Bench to 80.7%, while WMDP-Bio and ProtocolQA decline versus Grok 4.5.",
      "pages": [32, 33, 34],
      "document": "xai-grok-4-6"
    },
    {
      "text": "Jailbreak results are mixed: standard jailbreak compliance improves to 0.04%, StrongReject worsens to 3.9%, and long-horizon jailbreak compliance is 1.0%.",
